# Horologe Genève — agent rules

- Use **JavaScript only** (no TypeScript) unless the user explicitly asks otherwise.
- Prefer **App Router** pages under `app/` and shared chrome in `components/`.
- Preserve Stitch design tokens and Tailwind theme classes from `app/globals.css` (`surface`, `on-surface`, `secondary`, spacing tokens, etc.).
- Keep brand pages visually aligned with Stitch screens; reuse `/public/stitch` assets.
- Link auth flows: `/login` ↔ `/register`; product detail at `/product`.
- Do not commit secrets (API keys in local MCP config stay outside the repo).
- Prefer small, focused diffs; avoid drive-by refactors.
